# English additions, loaded on top of tbl/jp.tbl (rombuild.en_table()): later lines win for decoding, and every
# character still encodes. Glyphs: font/en_glyphs.txt (tools/font.py). A-Z (A2-BB) and 0-9 (C6-CF) keep their
# jp.tbl codes and are redrawn; lowercase and punctuation use the free glyph codes D0-F6 (docs/re/text.md §Font).
BF=+
C0=?
C1=!
C2=~
D0=a
D1=b
D2=c
D3=d
D4=e
D5=f
D6=g
D7=h
D8=i
D9=j
DA=k
DB=l
DC=m
DD=n
DE=o
DF=p
E0=q
E1=r
E2=s
E3=t
E4=u
E5=v
E6=w
E7=x
E8=y
E9=z
EA=.
EB=,
EC='
ED="
EE=-
EF=:
F0=;
F1=(
F2=)
F3=&
F4=/
F5=%
F6=…
